---
// "You have changes you haven't saved" — raised by scripts/dashboard/unsaved-guard.ts.
//
// **Words, not a marker, and that was a decision (owner, 2026-08-05).** The first attempt put a
// coloured dot on the tab. He rejected it, and the reason is the one that matters: the site already
// uses that exact dot for unread messages, so it read as "something is waiting for you to deal with
// it" — and a seller who has never met an editor's unsaved-document convention has no way to learn
// what a second dot means. A notice can only work here if it says what it means in a sentence.
//
// Floating, for the reason StaleDataBar's own header gives:
// it appears while the seller is mid-task, so a bar at the top of the page would either be
// off-screen behind a long table or shove the thing they are reading. It also has to be visible
// from EVERY tab, which is the whole complaint that started this — panels are hidden, not
// destroyed, so an edit in Settings survives a trip to Products with nothing on screen saying so.
//
// It never saves anything. Pressing it carries the seller TO the save button and focuses it; a
// floating control that submitted a form they cannot see would be the opposite of clarity.
//
// **The thing that carries them there is the section's NAME, underlined, inside the sentence** —
// there is no second "קח אותי לשם" button any more (owner, סשן א׳ §3: *"ושם הלשונית עם קו תחתון
// מתחתיה והיא לחיצה, בלי ׳קח אותי לשם׳"*). The sentence already names the one place the press could
// possibly mean, so a button repeating it in a verb was a second subject for one destination — and
// two of these bars can be out at once, each ending in the same three words.
//
// It is `bottom-6` at rest and `scripts/dashboard/bar-stack.ts` moves it when another bar is out —
// the offsets used to be reserved per bar, which left a gap whenever a reserved slot was empty.
// Each bar still positions ITSELF rather than sharing a flex container: the elevation guard wants
// the element casting a shadow to declare that it floats, and an ancestor cannot vouch for it.
//
// Hidden with the `!hidden` utility, not the `hidden` attribute: this element is display:flex and a
// flex utility beats the attribute's display:none (the trap is documented across the dashboard).
---

<div
  id="dash-unsaved-bar"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
  class="!hidden fixed bottom-6 inset-x-4 z-[9998] flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1.5 py-2 px-3 rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] border [border-color:var(--color-border)] [background:var(--color-surface)] shadow-[var(--shadow-card)] text-[0.82rem] sm:inset-x-auto sm:left-1/2 sm:-translate-x-1/2 sm:max-w-[calc(100vw-2rem)] sm:flex-nowrap sm:gap-3 sm:py-[0.55rem] sm:px-[0.9rem] sm:text-[0.85rem]" data-bottom-bar
>
    {/* Icon and sentence are ONE flex item, and its `basis` is what decides where the row breaks
        on a phone: given 12rem to start from, a short line still leaves room for its buttons beside
        it, and a long one pushes them onto their own row instead of squeezing the words into a
        column three lines tall. `grow` then lets the sentence take whatever is left. Above `sm` it
        is an ordinary flex child and everything sits on one line. */}
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 min-w-0 grow basis-[12rem] sm:basis-auto sm:flex-1 sm:gap-3">
    <svg class="shrink-0 max-w-none [color:var(--color-warning)]" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M19 21H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11l5 5v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2z"/><polyline points="17 21 17 13 7 13 7 21"/><polyline points="7 3 7 8 15 8"/>
    </svg>
  {/* The sentence is assembled from three server-rendered pieces rather than written into one span,
      so the section's name can be a real control without any script building markup: the guard sets
      three strings and nothing else. `unsaved-guard.ts#refreshUnsavedNotice` fills them. */}
  <span id="dash-unsaved-msg" class="min-w-0">
    <span data-notice-pre></span
    ><button
      type="button"
      id="dash-unsaved-go"
      class="p-0 bg-transparent border-0 font-[inherit] text-[inherit] cursor-pointer underline underline-offset-[3px] [color:var(--color-text)] transition-colors duration-100 hover:[color:var(--color-primary)]"
    ></button
    ><span data-notice-post></span>
    </span>
  </div>
</div>
